    <!-- ADDITIONAL SETUP FOR EXPANSIONS -->
	<div id="additional-setup-for-expansions">
		<div class="rules-box">
			<h4>ADDITIONAL SETUP FOR EXPANSIONS</h4>
			<div class="note-box">NOTE:
				<ul>
					<li>Most Expansions will only require You to Shuffle the new Cards into the Deck.</li>
					<li>Here is a List of all Expansions that may require Additional Setup Steps</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>OBLIVION EXPANSION:</strong> Choose whether to include the Revealing Trap Class Chaos Card.</li>
				<li><strong>SINGULARITY EXPANSION:</strong> Choose whether to include the Revealing Trap Class Chaos Card.
					<div class="tip-box"> TIP: Shuffle the 3 SOL/OVE/RSE cards into the Deck separately to each other to avoid Drawing more than 1 of them in succession.</div>
				</li>
				<li><strong>CRISIS EXPANSION:</strong>
					<ol>
						<li>Add 1 x Crisis Trap Class Chaos Card for each Player + 1 extra to the Deck before initial Shuffling and Dealing.</li>
						<li>Choose a Special Victory Condition before starting.</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li><strong>CONTAGION EXPANSION:</strong> Remove both Poison Trap Class Chaos Cards from the Core Game [and the one from the Core Booster Pack if You have it], as it has been re-released with a new design in this Expansion Pack.</li>
			</ul>
			<div class="return-link-wrapper">
				<a href="#top" class="return-link">🔝 Return to Rulebook Contents</a>
			</div>
    	</div>
	</div>

     <!-- HOW TO PLAY -->
	<div id="how-to-play">
		<div class="rules-box">
			<h4>HOW TO PLAY</h4>
			<ol>
				<li>Determine who goes First, then each Player Draws 5 Cards.</li>
				<li>Next, reveal 1 Card from the Tier 1 Trade Deck for each Player in the Game, forming the last, Tier 1 Trade Row.
					<div class="note-box">NOTE: Now from Left to Right-Top to Bottom, Your setup should have a Grid of 4 Trade Rows, then 4 Tiered Trade Decks, then the Chaos Draw +10ST Face-Up with the 3 Random Chaos Draw +10’s Face-Down underneath it.</div>
				</li>
				<li>On Your Turn, play Cards from your Hand in front of you. Once this is done, you cannot put it back in your Hand.
					<ol type="a">
						<li>0-9 Coloured Number Cards [XP] allows you to Buy Cards in the various Tiered Trade Rows based on the following Costs:
							<ol type="i">
								<li><strong style="color: var(--color-card-class);">Tier 1:</strong> A minimum XP of the Face Value of the Numbered Card shown.
									<div class="advanced-box">ADVANCED NOTE: Use just one of these or both for an increased challenge.
										<ul>
											<li>Tier 1 Trade Row XP Cards that match Your chosen Personal Deck’s Colour are 2XP cheaper for Yourself.</li>
											<li>Tier 1 Trade Row XP Cards that do NOT match Your chosen Personal Deck’s Colour are 2XP more expensive for Yourself.</li>
										</ul>
									</div>
								</li>
								<li><strong style="color: var(--color-card-class);">Tier 2:</strong> 3XP.</li>
								<li><strong style="color: var(--color-card-class);">Tier 3:</strong> 5XP + Discard Any 1 Chaos Card.</li>
								<li><strong style="color: var(--color-card-class);">Tier 4:</strong> 7XP + Discard Any 2 Chaos Cards.</li>
							</ol>
							<div class="note-box">NOTES:
								<ul>
									<li>Unless otherwise stated, any Cards Purchased [including if Purchased for Free], must be placed in your Discards.</li>
									<li>If, after Purchasing a Card from Tier 1-3 Trade Decks, you reveal a Trap Class Chaos Card, resolve its Effects then Scrap it.</li>
								</ul>
							</div>
							<div class="important-box">IMPORTANT: There are no Refunds. Once an XP Card is used to Buy a Card from any Trade Row, that Card can no longer be used that Turn.</div>
							<div class="example-box">EXAMPLE: You Play 3 and 4 XP Cards and buy a Card worth 5 XP. Those XP Cards are now considered Used and Cannot be used towards other Purchases.</div>
						</li>
						<li>0 XP Card: Allows you to Scrap any Card in Your Discards. Potentially Strengthening Your Personal Deck, making it easier to Draw the Cards You need.</li>
						<li>Reverse Action Class Card: Reverses Play. Then Forces all other Players to Discard 1 Card [Hand and/or Table] immediately.
							<div class="note-box">NOTE: Reverse and similar Effects always activate before Effects similar to Skip.</div>
						</li>
						<li>Skip Action Class Card: Skips the next Player’s Turn. They Discard Their Hand and Redraw. Then allows You to Draw 1 Card and set it aside until the Start of Your next Turn.
							<div class="note-box">NOTE: If playing more than 1 Skip Effect, They do not Stack on that Target but continues to Skip each subsequent Player instead.</div>
							<div class="example-box">EXAMPLE: You Play 2 Skip Effect Cards, Skipping the next 2 Players’ Turns.</div>
						</li>
						<li>Draw +2 Action Class Card: Allows you to Draw 2 Cards this Turn.</li>
						<li>Chaos Cards: Follow their Effects based on the (09-A) Soloverse - Deck-Builder (Definitions Rulebook).</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>You will also need to Level Up Your Personal Deck to Win:
					<ul>
						<li><strong style="color: var(--color-card-class);">LV1:</strong> You Start on LV1 with your Coloured Draw +2.</li>
						<li><strong style="color: var(--color-card-class);">LV2:</strong> On any Turn You have in Your Hand:
							<ul>
								<li>Your Coloured Draw +2 to Play.</li>
								<li>A minimum of 4XP to Play.</li>
								<li>Plus, any 1 Chaos Card to Discard.</li>
							</ul>
							You may Purchase Your Random Chaos Draw +2 and add it to Your Discards.
						</li>
						<li><strong style="color: var(--color-card-class);">LV3:</strong> On any Turn You have in Your Hand:
							<ul>
								<li>Your Random Draw +2 to Play.</li>
								<li>A minimum of 6XP to Play.</li>
								<li>Plus, any 1 Chaos Card to Discard.</li>
							</ul>
							You may Purchase Your Random Chaos Draw +3 and add it to Your Discards.
						</li>
						<li><strong style="color: var(--color-card-class);">LV4:</strong> On any Turn You have in Your Hand:
							<ul>
								<li>Your Random Draw +3 to Play.</li>
								<li>A minimum of 8XP to Play.</li>
								<li>Plus, any 1 Chaos Card to Discard.</li>
							</ul>
							You may Purchase Your Random Chaos Draw +4 and add it to Your Discards.
						</li>
						<li><strong style="color: var(--color-card-class);">LV5:</strong> On any Turn You have in Your Hand:
							<ul>
								<li>Your Random Draw +4 to Play.</li>
								<li>A minimum of 10XP to Play.</li>
								<li>Plus, any 1 Chaos Card to Discard.</li>
							</ul>
							You may Purchase Your Random Chaos Draw +5 and add it to Your Discards.
							<div class="victory-box">
								VICTORY CONDITION NOTE: This CAN Win You the Game if this Victory Condition was chosen at the Start of the Game.
								If NOT, Continue with the following:
							</div>
						</li>
						<li><strong style="color: var(--color-card-class);">LV6:</strong> On any Turn You have in Your Hand:
							<ul>
								<li>Your Random Draw +5 to Play.</li>
								<li>A minimum of 20XP to Play.</li>
								<li>Plus, any 1 Chaos Card to Discard.</li>
							</ul>
							You may Purchase a Random Chaos Draw +10 from the Table and add it to Your Discards.
							<div class="note-box">NOTE: If Playing with more than 3 Players, once the last Random Chaos Draw +10 is Gained, all other Players instantly Lose.</div>
						</li>
						<li><strong style="color: var(--color-card-class);">LV7:</strong> On any Turn You have in Your Hand:
							<ul>
								<li>Your Random Draw +10 to Play.</li>
								<li>A minimum of 20XP to Play.</li>
								<li>Plus, any 2 Chaos Cards to Discard.</li>
							</ul>
							You may Purchase the Winning Chaos Draw +10 Specific Targeted and add it to Your Discards.
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>Once any chosen Cards have been Played and their Effects finalised, placed any Cards left in your Hand and those you Played into your Discards and Draw 5 more Cards</li>
				<li>When You need to continue Drawing and Your Personal Deck is empty, Shuffle Your Discards to re-form your Personal Deck.</li>
				<li>Then end your Turn.</li>
			</ol>
			<div class="return-link-wrapper">
				<a href="#top" class="return-link">🔝 Return to Rulebook Contents</a>
			</div>	
		</div>
	</div>

    <!-- VICTORY CONDITIONS -->
	<div id="victory-conditions">
		<div class="rules-box">
			<h4>VICTORY CONDITIONS</h4>
			<ol>
				<li>Obtaining either the <strong>Chaos Draw +5</strong> or the <strong>Chaos Draw +10 Specific Targeted</strong> [depending on Your choice at the Start of the Game] Wins You the Game!</li>
				<li>Special Victory Conditions.
					<ul>
						<li>Some Expansions have Special Victory Conditions that exceed the normal means of Winning. For example:
							<ol type="a">
								<li>The Singularity Expansion allows You to collect all 3 Unification Class Chaos Cards.</li>
								<li>While the Crisis Expansion Crisis Class Chaos Cards allow for many different Special Victory Conditions.</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
						<li>In any of these situations, doing so automatically, and instantly, Wins You the game!</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>The game ends Without a Clear Winner.
					<ol type="a">
						<li>The game ends Without a Clear Winner [such as all Tiered Trade Rows run out of Gainable Cards]. In any situation without a clear Winner:
							<ol type="i">
								<li>The Player with the Highest Levelled Personal Deck Wins.</li>
								<li>If Players have an Equal Personal Deck Level, the Player with the Highest Total of Chaos Cards in Their Personal Deck Wins.</li>
								<li>If Players have an Equal amount of Chaos Cards in Their Personal Deck, the Player with the Highest Total XP in Their Personal Deck Wins.</li>
								<li>If Players have an Equal Total XP left in Their Personal Decks, Congrats! It must have been a Great Game!! All remaining Players separate Their Level Up Deck [Coloured Draw +2 to Random Chaos Draw +5], Shuffle them and reveal the Top Card at the same time. The Player with the Highest Value Draw Card Wins!</li>
								<li>If that’s still not enough, repeat the process until you find a Winner [I mean, at this point, you must be desperate].</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<div class="return-link-wrapper">
				<a href="#top" class="return-link">🔝 Return to Rulebook Contents</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>

	<!-- Soloverse Rulebook Page Engine: Auto-Theme Detection and Update Sync -->
    <script is:inline>
        (function() {
            // 1. SERVICE WORKER REVALIDATION
            if ('serviceWorker' in navigator) {
                navigator.serviceWorker.getRegistrations().then(function(registrations) {
                    for (let registration of registrations) {
                        registration.update(); 
                    }
                });
            }

            // 2. AUTOMATED THEME EVALUATION (User Override vs System Preference)
            const savedTheme = localStorage.getItem('soloverse-theme');
            const devicePrefersDarkMode = window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches;
            
            let activeTheme = 'dark'; // Base anchor default fallback

            if (savedTheme) {
                activeTheme = savedTheme;
            } else {
                activeTheme = devicePrefersDarkMode ? 'dark' : 'light';
            }

            // Mount theme instantly to root document element
            document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', activeTheme);
        })();
    </script>
